{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Test-count parity BASELINE recorded (for the successor)\n\nThe plan requires full-suite test-count parity per split against each change's parent commit.\nThat baseline was measured before the session stopped, on a **clean tree** at\n`2af5a4c773925336d38697b1bb681a6fd70ce9cd` (the worktree HEAD = `origin/main` at the time),\nwith the exact CI-parity selection the plan names:\n\n    pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 3 --dist worksteal --timeout=300\n\n    12834 passed, 60 skipped, 24 warnings in 1384.00s (0:23:03)   exit 0\n\n**0 failed, 0 errors.** Note the clean run has NO `_no_repo_commits` teardown errors — the\nguard trips only when a `git commit`/`--amend` lands while the suite is in flight (see\n`defaceable-icy-antelope`'s note). If a successor sees `Test moved the repo HEAD (...)` errors,\nthat is their own commit overlapping the run, not a regression: check that zero tests FAILED.\n\nTwo caveats on reusing this number:\n\n1. It is only a valid parity baseline while the parent commit is `2af5a4c773`. Several changes\n   were in flight at measurement time (1730, 1735, 1736, 1737, 1738, 1742) and at least 1735\n   (`effete-barbaric-xiaosaurus`) has since closed. **Re-measure at the actual parent commit**\n   before claiming parity — the absolute count moves as those land.\n2. Both splits are pure relocations, so the expected delta is exactly **0**. A non-zero delta\n   means a test module stopped being collected — most likely an import that no longer resolves\n   because a re-export was missed. That is the signal the parity check exists to catch, and it\n   is the cheapest detector of the monkeypatch/re-export traps described in the handoff comment.\n"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786656136796085001,"uuid":"287d7638-c228-4423-9497-39d8c1ded071"}